{"term":"recent","senses":[{"id":"kaikki:19aad19bed79c5c73e","definition":"Having happened a short while ago.","example":"Bats host many high-profile viruses that can infect humans, including severe acute respiratory syndrome and Ebola. A recent study explored the ecological variables that may contribute to bats’ propensity to harbor such zoonotic diseases by comparing them with another order of common reservoir hosts: rodents.","pos":"adj","synonyms":["nudiustertian"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["non-recent","nonrecent","recency","Recent","recentish","recentism","recently","recent memory","in recent memory","recentness","semirecent","subrecent","unrecent"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recent#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:8963b03e10100ffb17","definition":"Up-to-date; not old-fashioned or dated.","example":"","pos":"adj","synonyms":["nouveau"],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["non-recent","nonrecent","recency","Recent","recentish","recentism","recently","recent memory","in recent memory","recentness","semirecent","subrecent","unrecent"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":"https://en.wiktionary.org/wiki/recent#English","license":"CC-BY-SA-4.0"},{"id":"kaikki:eaab80421de55b4aed","definition":"Having done something a short while ago that distinguishes them as what they are called.","example":"The cause has several hundred recent donors.","pos":"adj","synonyms":[],"antonyms":[],"collocations":[],"usage":"","register":"","wordFamily":["non-recent","nonrecent","recency","Recent","recentish","recentism","recently","recent memory","in recent memory","recentness","semirecent","subrecent","unrecent"],"source":"English Wiktionary via Kaikki.org","attribution":"English Wiktionary contributors","sourceUrl":